            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the infiltration test we notice some air leakage from the followings house components:

- Window in the bathromm ( the one located between the bedrooms)

- The main entrance door, the garage door and the exterior door in the laundry room.

- The receptacles

- The fireplace 



Air leakage contribute to heat loss and lower the interior temperature. The warm air is replaced by the cold air, this situation increase the energy required to heat the interior space and also lower the humidity inside the house.



We recommend the replacement of the weather strips of all windows and doors and insulator in the receptacles. Concerning the fireplace we recommend to consult a specialist to seal properly the hedges of the heating unit.</airSeal>
                <VentilationSystem>In this moment the house is not equipped with a ventilation unit. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator)  certified HVI (Home Ventilation Institute). This type of equipment will contribute to increase the air quality of the house and give you a better control of the humidty inside the living space.</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
